/*!
    \page creator-how-to-collect-usage-statistics.html
    \previouspage creator-how-tos.html

    \ingroup creator-how-to-use

    \title Collect usage statistics

    When you install \QC with \QOI, you can allow it to collect pseudonymous
    information about your system and \QC use. If you decline, the telemetry
    plugin is not installed and no usage statistics are collected.

    \section1 Principles of data collection

    No personal data, such as names, IP addresses, MAC addresses, or project
    and path names are collected. However, QUuid objects are used to identify
    data records that belong to one user. The objects cannot be converted
    back to the actual values from which they were generated.

    For more information about Qt privacy policy, see
    \l{Qt Appendix for Privacy and Security}.

   \QC respects the same privacy rules.

    \section1 Turn on data collection

    To allow the telemetry plugin to collect data, go to \preferences >
    \uicontrol Telemetry > \uicontrol {Usage Statistics}, and then select
    \uicontrol {Send pseudonymous usage statistics}.

    \image {qtcreator-preferences-telemetry-usage-statistics.webp} {Usage Statistics tab in Telemetry preferences}

    \section1 Collected data

    \QC collects the following data:

    \list
        \li Your Qt license.
        \li The selected \QC theme and UI language, and the system locale.
        \li The modes that you use.
        \li Information about what you use to build your projects:
            \list
                \li The Qt version.
                \li The Qt and QML modules.
                \li The build system (CMake, qmake, and so on).
                \li The build and run device types.
                \li The compiler and debugger types and versions.
            \endlist
        \li The Qt examples that you opened.
        \li The \QC wizards that you used.
        \li How you use the profiler: which recording backend you used, whether
            the recording succeeded and how many seconds it lasted, and the
            format of the traces that you opened. The names and paths of the
            programs you profile and of your traces are not collected.
        \li How you move through the profiler: whether you are on the page for
            starting a recording, in a running recording, or in a trace, the
            trace format, and which view of the trace you switch to.
    \endlist

    \section1 Qt Profiler

    The standalone Qt Profiler application can collect the profiler data
    listed above if it was built with support for it. It asks for your consent
    when you start it for the first time. To change your choice later, select
    \uicontrol {Usage Statistics} in the toolbar. Qt Profiler does not collect
    data when it runs in a script or when \QC hosts it, and \QC then collects
    it as described above.

    The code is available at \l{qt-creator/plugin-telemetry.git}.

    \sa {Installation}
*/
